<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beka I Jaqeli</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Beka Jaqeli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beka I Jaqeli was atabeg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samtskhe">Samtskhe</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in the late 13th and early 14th centuries. Ruling under Mongol overlordship, he strengthened the autonomy of his principality and issued a law code that was later expanded under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v">George V</a> and is known as the Code of Beka and Aghbugha, an important monument of Georgian law.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beka-i-jaqeli.jpg" alt="Beka I Jaqeli" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 14th century CE · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_Beka_I_Jaqeli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
